./.mpd/team/archive/rtl-gap-assessment/team.json:216:      "output": "INVENTORY: my-power-dsh RTL-relevant capabilities (read-only, evidence-backed)\n\n## 1. Shipped surface (what the bundle is)\n- Preset `mpd` (packages/mpd-bootstrap-plugin/presets/mpd/preset.yml + agent.cordis.yml): host tools bash/pwsh, fs (read/write/edit), fs-search (glob/grep), jobs, skill, goal, plan-mode, compaction, subagents (subagent/subagent_fork/interrupt/list/send), workflow, ralph, ask_user_question, todo_write, web_search; tool presentation native.\n- Bundle patch rows (packages/mpd-bundle/cordis.patch.yml): 4 local MCP rows (mcp-astgrep, mcp-gitbash [disabled, Windows-only], mcp-lsp, mcp-codegraph) + 2 remote MCP rows (context7, grep_app) + 13 plugin rows (mpd-web-compat, mpd-config, mpd-tools, mpd-modelchain, mpd-roles, mpd-ulw, mpd-hashline, mpd-boulder, mpd-comment-checker, mpd-codegraph, mpd-memory, mpd-workmate, mpd-bootstrap) + adopted agent-teams row (mpd roster profile, 11 normal-named specialist members, agent_teams_* tools + Web panel).\n- mpd_* tools (~30): mpd_boulder_* (6), mpd_comment_check, mpd_config_get/reload, mpd_hashline_* (4), mpd_memory_* (7), mpd_modelchain_resolve, mpd_roles_list/role_spawn/role_persona, mpd_ultrawork/mpd_ulw, mpd_workmate_* (4) — all generic process/workflow disciplines, none language-specific.\n- Skills shipped (19, copied to $DSH_HOME/skills at boot): ast-grep, coding-agent-sessions, data-scientist, debugging, dsh-qa, frontend, git-master, init-deep, lsp-setup, programming, refactor, remove-ai-slops, review-work, svn-master, ultimate-browsing, ulw-execute, ulw-plan, ulw-research, visual-qa. NONE is RTL-specific (no Verilog/SystemVerilog skill; programming covers .py/.rs/.ts/.go only; lsp-setup has no HDL route; svn-master is VCS-relevant for chip flows).\n\n## 2. Language-support surface (evidence — the decisive gap)\n- ast-grep MCP: exactly 25 languages, NO Verilog/SystemVerilog (skills/ast-grep/scripts/ast_grep_helper.py langs output).\n- LSP MCP: BUILTIN_SERVERS ~33 (packages/mpd-mcp-lsp/dist/cli.js lines ~3610-3710: ts/js/deno/vue/eslint/oxlint/biome/gopls/ruby/py/elixir/zig/c#/f#/swift/rust/clangd/svelte/astro/bash/jdtls/yaml/lua/php/dart/terraform/prisma/ocaml/tex/dockerfile/gleam/clojure/nix/typst/haskell/kotlin/julia/razor). NO Verilog/SystemVerilog server (no verible, svls, slang, hdl_checker). No custom-server config seam found in vendored upstream lsp-tools-mcp/lsp-daemon.\n- codegraph MCP: v1.5.0 ships exactly 29 tree-sitter grammars (wasm list under .tmp-cache/.../@colbymchenry/codegraph-linux-x64@1.5.0/lib/dist/extraction/wasm/), grep -c -i verilog = 0 in the bundle. Cannot index .v/.sv.\n- context7 + grep_app: remote; grep_app (GitHub code search) CAN retrieve real-world Verilog/SystemVerilog examples (language filter free-form) — the only RTL-code-discovery channel.\n\n## 3. RTL-adjacent assets that DO exist (evidence)\n- Golden Verilog fixtures: tests/golden/fixtures/verilog/{modules/adder4.v, modules/cnt8.v, tb/tb_adder4.v} + reference docs docs/adder4.md, docs/cnt8.md. Task README (tests/golden/fixtures/verilog/README.md) explicitly says \"No simulator needed; the file must be syntactically valid Verilog-2001\" → write-only, NO executable validation.\n- P5 golden batch evidence (evidence/p5/rubric.md): G2 adder4 PASS 87/100 (codegraph crash noise), G4 doc PASS 100, G9 cnt8 PASS 100 — proves the bundle can WRITE well-commented synthesizable Verilog text, but nothing ever compiled/simulated/linted it.\n- evidence/p5/golden-g2.log: codegraph ENOENT mkdir ~/.omo/codegraph spam in sandbox (F13 finding: codegraph excluded under path policy).\n- dsh-qa skill case table (skills/dsh-qa/SKILL.md): zero RTL cases; evidence/dsh-qa/ has no RTL domain.\n\n## 4. What is genuinely usable for RTL today (generic)\nbash (any HDL toolchain the user has: iverilog/vcs/verilator/yosys via shell), read/write/edit (plain text), glob/grep, hashline anchored edits (discipline on any text file), memory/VCS (git + svn-master skill), subagents/teams/workflow for parallel flow automation, dsh-qa evidence discipline, bilingual docs convention. But nothing HDL-aware: no grammar, no HDL LSP, no simulator/lint/waveform/coverage/synthesis integration, no RTL skills, no flow automation (fusesoc/edalize/Makefile) helpers.\n\n## 5. Gap handoff (for Architect t3)\nGap classes to map: (1) HDL-aware editing/lint (Verible/svls/slang LSP, ast-grep SV grammar), (2) simulation & waveform (iverilog/verilator/VCS + VCD/FST viewing), (3) verification (UVM/SVA/assertions, constrained-random, coverage), (4) synthesis/CDC/UPF (yosys, SpyGlass-like), (5) project/flow automation (filelist/build/Makefile/fusesoc/edalize), (6) RTL skill corpus + golden testbench scaffolding, (7) codegraph/ast-grep extension for SV. Evidence files: see sections above; all paths absolute under /root/dshProj/my-power-dsh."
./.mpd/team/archive/rtl-gap-assessment/team.json:231:      "output": "# t3 — Gap framework + AI-RTL feedback-loop analysis (Architect, read-only)\n\nGrounding: bundle patch `packages/mpd-bundle/cordis.patch.yml` (rows: mcp-astgrep/lsp/codegraph/context7/grepapp + mpd-* plugins + agent-teams profile), ast-grep language enum (no Verilog/SV), `skills/lsp-setup/references/` (no verilog dir), skills corpus listing (no HDL skill), `tests/golden/fixtures/verilog/` (adder4.v, cnt8.v, tb_adder4.v — \"No simulator needed\"), docs/adder4.md + cnt8.md.\n\n## 1. Analysis framework (for the synthesis task)\n\nThree dimensions cross-applied to the six workflow surfaces (coding assistance, lint/style, sim/waveform/coverage, verification, synthesis/CDC/UPF, project/flow automation):\n\n- **D1 — loop stage**: codegen → syntax/lint gate → elaboration/sim gate → coverage/waveform evidence → prompt improvement.\n- **D2 — capability ladder**: Host/LLM native → generic tool usable for RTL → RTL-aware (generic tool configured for HDL) → RTL-dedicated (HDL-specific tool). Ladder shows *how far* each gap is from closure, not just whether.\n- **D3 — evidence contract**: every gap claim cites a bundle fact (patch row, tool language enum, skills dir listing) or an explicit absence-argument (documented supported-language list that omits HDL). Status scale: ✅ present w/ evidence / 🟡 partial (manual config needed) / ❌ absent / ➖ not bundle-relevant.\n\nRisk tiering rule: **BLOCKING** = a loop step whose absence breaks the minimum viable RTL loop (codegen→check→sim). **HIGHLY VALUABLE** = improves throughput/confidence but the loop still runs without it. **NOT bundle-relevant** = host-level, license/legal, compute.\n\n## 2. Closed-loop analysis (AI-generated RTL)\n\n| Loop step | Status | Evidence / mechanism to close |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Codegen | ✅ (LLM native) | DeepSeek dual track; Verilog support is model capability |\n| 2. Syntax/lint gate | ❌ BLOCKING | ast-grep supports no Verilog/SV (language enum ends at yaml); `lsp-setup/references/` has no verilog/systemverilog entry; no iverilog `-tnull` / verilator `--lint-only` / verible wrapper. Shipped golden fixtures are never syntax-checked — their README admits \"No simulator needed\". Loop breaks here. |\n| 3. Elaboration/sim gate | ❌ BLOCKING | No simulator MCP (iverilog/verilator/yosys), no tb-run wrapper, no pass/fail capture. AI-generated RTL today is unverifiable inside the bundle. |\n| 4. Coverage/waveform evidence | ❌ BLOCKING | No coverage collection, no VCD→waveform/regression diff; memory plugin can store evidence but nothing produces RTL evidence. |\n| 5. Prompt improvement | 🟡 partial | mpd-memory (git-backed + reflection) stores lessons generically; no RTL-specific feedback channel (lint/sim failure → prompt notes → re-run). Golden fixtures + dsh-qa could host regression gates but no executable gate exists. |\n| Cross-cut: LSP for SV | 🟡 | `mcp-lsp` daemon is generic; wiring `verible-verilog-ls` / `svls` / `hdl_checker` is config-only (lsp-setup reference). |\n| Cross-cut: codegraph for SV | 🟡 | generic index, no .sv/.v grammar evidence in plugin src; treat as text-level until verified. grep_app (open-source RTL search) and context7 (docs) are present and genuinely useful. |\n\n**Usage-mode lens** (the adoption angle):\n- *AI-generated RTL*: minimum viable loop = generate → parse/lint → sim → evidence → prompt fix. Today only step 1 exists in-bundle; steps 2–5 happen manually outside the bundle → \"vibe coding\" with zero feedback is unsafe for an IC engineer.\n- *Verification assistant*: today = testbench/assertion codegen only; to be an assistant rather than a writer it needs run + coverage + failure triage (steps 2–4).\n- *Flow automation*: ulw/boulder/team/memory give the orchestration substrate ✅; missing are RTL-aware flow gates (lint/sim as ulw criteria, filelist/make scaffolds). Host bash tool can run CLIs manually — the gap is structured gating, not raw capability.\n- *Dual toolchain*: open stack (iverilog/verilator/yosys/cocotb) is fully bundle-able as PATH/env-resolved wrappers; commercial stack (VCS/Xcelium/Verdi/DC/Spyglass) is license-gated and SUL-1.0 non-commercial → supported only as user-env command wrappers, never bundled.\n\n## 3. Risk tiers\n\n**BLOCKING (minimum loop cannot close)**\n1. HDL syntax/elaboration gate (verilator `--lint-only` / iverilog `-tnull` / verible).\n2. Simulator + testbench run gate with pass/fail evidence (iverilog/verilator).\n3. Waveform/coverage regression evidence (VCD→text/JSON diff) — closes step 4 so prompts can improve.\n4. RTL skill codifying the loop + golden-fixture regression discipline.\n\n**HIGHLY VALUABLE, OPTIONAL**\n5. Verilog/SV LSP wiring (verible-verilog-ls, svls, hdl_checker) in lsp-setup.\n6. codegraph .sv/.v support (verify + document).\n7. UVM/SV verification-assistant skill (SV patterns, assertion templates).\n8. EDA flow-automation scaffolds (filelist/make, synthesis/CDC/UPF CLI wrappers by env path).\n9. RTL workmate template (persona: RTL verification, sim-gate discipline).\n\n**NOT bundle-relevant**\n- Commercial EDA license management (legal/licensing), simulation-farm compute, GUI waveform viewers on desktop (GTKWave/Verdi — host-level), proprietary PDK/IP access. SUL-1.0 constraints mean commercial wrappers are user-side only.\n\n## 4. Integration patterns (respecting SUL-1.0 / upstream-parity / minimal-diffs)\n\n- **Pattern A — MCP rows wrapping CLI tools (preferred for gates)**: same shape as `mcp-astgrep` (dsh-mcp-client stdio → small CLI shelling out to iverilog/verilator/verible), binary resolved from PATH or `MPD_DSH_*` env, graceful degradation when absent. Do **not** vendor GPL binaries; system-resolve instead (matches ast-grep convention).\n- **Pattern B — custom skill**: `skills/rtl-dev` (SKILL.md + references + golden fixtures + dsh-qa case script). Skills are the sanctioned knowledge layer and ship via mpd-bootstrap. Cheapest highest-value move.\n- **Pattern C — LSP wiring (config-only)**: extend `lsp-setup/references/` with verilog/systemverilog; the mpd-mcp-lsp daemon is generic, no plugin change needed.\n- **Pattern D — codegraph for SV**: verify extension/grammar coverage; low priority vs LSP.\n- **Pattern E — new mpd plugin only when a *stateful gate* must be enforced** (e.g., lint+sim must pass before workmate/ulw completion). Otherwise plain wrappers — Principle 6 (minimal diffs).\n- **Recommended order**: B (skill) → A (sim/lint MCP) → C (LSP refs) → later E (enforce gates). Net-new surface beyond upstream parity is acceptable here (goal explicitly requests RTL assessment), but this task makes no code changes.\n\n## 5. Prioritization grid skeleton (impact × effort; final numbers belong to synthesis)\n\n| P | Item | Impact | Effort |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P0 | Verilog/SV syntax+lint gate (verilator/iverilog/verible wrapper) | High | S–M |\n| P0 | Simulator MCP + tb run + pass/fail evidence (.mpd evidence + memory) | High | M |\n| P0 | `skills/rtl-dev` loop discipline + golden-fixture regression | High | S |\n| P1 | Verilog/SV LSP reference (verible-verilog-ls/svls) | Med-High | S |\n| P1 | Waveform/coverage evidence (VCD→JSON diff regression) | Med | M |\n| P1 | cocotb/verilator coverage harness pattern in skill | Med | M |\n| P1 | codegraph .sv support verify + doc | Low-Med | S |\n| P2 | EDA flow scaffolds (filelist/make, CDC/UPF wrappers, commercial by env path) | Med | M–L |\n| P2 | UVM/SV verification-assistant skill | Med | M |\n| P2 | RTL workmate template | Low-Med | S |\n\nTop single recommendation: **close the P0 syntax→sim→evidence chain first (Patterns B+A)**; everything else is amplifier."
./.mpd/team/mpd-default-d92bc69a/team.json:264:      "output": "Delivered `evidence/rtl-extraction-residual/scope/acceptance.md` (382 lines, English): the checkable acceptance contract for \"the RTL surface is completely stripped from @mpd-dsh/mpd\", authored on the split's own governance record instead of a self-invented standard.\n\nBasis (pinned): mpd 32ae54dd10db7ea46e1c1263143d56f266fd1f78 (dev) + silicon bf3dae2530949d9fe410cec9b25b5581bdbcc58e. Authoritative rule = silicon docs/sync-policy.md §5 L83-91 (\"It must not keep: any copy of the RTL skill trees, the verif plugin, the LSP overlay, the RTL guides, the golden fixtures, or the profile data itself\") + §1 L14-23 (what mpd keeps: the rtl-ip carrier hook + a pointer note).\n\nBuckets (all four, each with concrete measured paths + explicit ruling): B1 FULL-STRIP = IN SCOPE; B2 BRIDGE-BY-DESIGN = IN SCOPE but conditional (needs a designating record + a resolving silicon target + registration + no assertion of the removed layout); B3 SILICON-CONTENT = OUT OF SCOPE as content / IN SCOPE as parity+resolution target; B4 UNTRACKED-BUILD-ARTIFACT = OUT OF SCOPE as repo content (a tracked path is never B4) / IN SCOPE as distribution hygiene.\n\n10 criteria C1..C10, every row carrying exact re-runnable commands and a formal-record citation (R1-R13 table with file:line or sha); inference register I1-I8 marks every non-quoted claim.\n\nMeasured residuals at the pin (t8 input, not a substitute for t1's ledger): (1) packages/mpd-mcp-lsp still ships HDL language-service content — templates/rtl-lsp-client.json present, verible/slang-server rows in overlay/lsp/{server-definitions,language-mappings}.ts and 4 hits in the built dist/cli.js, plus the README RTL section pointing at the references/verilog|systemverilog READMEs deleted by 32ae54d (dangling); (2) all six RTL guides still in docs/ (4 stale vs their corrected silicon twins, docs/index.md L19 still links one); (3) tests/golden/fixtures/verilog/** (4 files, byte-identical to silicon, zero live mpd consumer); (4) docs/adder4.md + docs/cnt8.md carry \"Source file: tests/golden/fixtures/verilog/...\" (follow-through if the fixtures move); (5) stale pack dist/mpd-package/skills/lsp-setup/references/{verilog,systemverilog}/README.md would install.\n\nBridge gaps (separate class, never residuals): the rtl-ip carrier hook required by sync-policy §1/§5 does NOT exist in mpd (0 hits for rtl-ip.profile.json in packages/scripts/presets; silicon t19 record L58 says \"the mpd-side carrier (task t15) has not landed\"), and README.md carries no \"RTL capability moved\" note; the live QA case rtl-verif.mjs has no SKILL.md case row while the rtl-ip-profile row (L62) still asserts the removed mpd-side layout. Also flagged: the standing reference gate accepts mpd's own checkout as a root, so it cannot alone prove no pre-strip mpd path survived; and a hash match is per-file sha256 parity — NOT evidence of an independent copy (measured: different inodes, link counts 1 vs 2).",
./.mpd/team/mpd-default-d92bc69a/team.json:636:      "output": "t9 done (Planner, design-only). Deliverables: evidence/rtl-extraction-residual/qa-standard/standard.md (normative software-type QA case standard: corpus rules C1-C7 with exact probe commands, case anatomy A1-A10, retirement rules R1-R6, the worked example, the ordered landing checklist for t8, open decisions) and inventory.md (all 25 case scripts classified + disposition, row<->script reconciliation, RTL golden assets with sha256 parity vs the silicon repo, the per-path inbound-reference map, explicit exemptions with reasons, coverage-owner table, acceptance instantiation for t11).\n\nWorked example is PROVEN, not asserted: raw/software-smoke.prototype.mjs (the landable bytes) passes --self-test offline (mutation control RED, 9 oracle violations) and its real lane boots a sandboxed mpd-headless session whose stub-driven write+bash tool calls really create and run a tiny deterministic game; the case replays the REAL bash transcript through its OWN oracle (legality/optimality/winner/determinism/content match) -> ok=true, sessions sandboxed. Landing = 2 deltas (repo-root form + ./lib/workspace-isolation.mjs import) documented in standard.md 5.6.\n\nMeasured facts for t8/t11: 25 scripts vs 24 SKILL.md rows -> C1 violated by dual-track-smoke vs llm-dual-track row, and rtl-verif has no row; the 2 RTL cases (rtl-verif, rtl-ip-profile) are the only silicon-coupled cases -> RETIRE with the RTL golden fixtures (tests/golden/fixtures/verilog/**, docs/adder4.md, docs/cnt8.md are sha256-IDENTICAL to silicon copies = no content loss); verify-rtl-references.mjs loses its only mpd-side subjects (CASES -> [], disclosure line required = green AND honest); one VENDOR_LOCK re-pin in the same commit as the skills change. Two captain decisions flagged: the 4 diverged RTL docs + dangling case ref (t20) and the workmate-library.mjs \"Verilog\" sample text exemption.",

